 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Each tree is a flat node list: node 0 is the root and node k is [text, children] where children lists node indices top to bottom; every node except the root has exactly one parent. A node with children has text \"\" and a node without children (a leaf label) has non-empty text. The word of a tree is the concatenation of its leaf texts in top-to-bottom (pre-order) order. Return true when the two trees spell the same word, even if the text is split differently across leaves.",
